OL,4,G1300FClassical Live
OL,5,     GLinton Stephens introduces an
OL,6,     Gafternoon of specially made
OL,7,     Grecordings, including music from
OL,8,     GLeipzig and chamber performances
OL,9,     Gfrom the BBC Radio 3 New
OL,10,     GGeneration Artists.
OL,11,G1500FChoral Evensong
OL,12,     GLive from Christ Church
OL,13,     GCathedral. Oxford, with music by
OL,14,     GTaverner, Palestrina, Victoria,
OL,15,     GMonteverdi and Buxtehude.
OL,16,G1600FComposer of the Week: Saint-Saens
OL,17,     GDonald Macleod follows Saint-
OL,18,     GSaens through the 1860s, from
OL,19,     Gpopular teacher with a growing
OL,20,     Gcircle of friends to the chaos of
OL,21,     Gwar which forces him in new
OL,22,     Gdirections.
